: Remove the additive response adapter, telemetry event, and focused tests.\n      observability: response-to-telemetry correlation test pass count\n---\n# Decision visibility\n\nSeparates enforcement from the externally visible reason and observation record.\n\n## Responsibility\n\nPresent a stable denial reason and emit matching decision telemetry.\n\n## Independent proof\n\nResponse and telemetry tests assert the same reason and decision identifier.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- **Emit a metric without returning a stable reason** — Callers could not distinguish limit denial from unrelated failures.\n\nThis derived seam is ready only while its cited evidence, named owner, contract,\nand rejected alternatives remain intact.\n=== seams/SEAM-POLICY-CONTRACT.md ===\n---\nschema_version: 1\nkind: seam\nclaim: derived\nid: SEAM-POLICY-CONTRACT\nname: Policy contract\ndescription: Separates accepted policy shape from resolution and enforcement.\nevidence:\n- E-BLUEPRINT\nresponsibility: Define and validate versioned organization rate-limit policy data.\nconsumes:\n- authored organization policy\nproduces:\n- validated policy document\nowner: platform-contracts\nindependent_proof: Invalid limits and windows fail schema validation deterministically.\ndecision_ids:\n- ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER\nrejected_alternatives:\n- alternative: Treat the API handler as the policy boundary\n  reason: Handler ownership would mix contract, resolution, and enforcement concerns.\nswimlane:\n  id: LANE-POLICY-CONTRACT\n  name: Policy contract lane\n  owner: platform-contracts\n  legs:\n  - id: LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID\n    observable_state: Rate-limit policy documents are schema-valid\n    proof: Invalid limits and windows are rejected; required fields are machine-readable.\n    requires: []\n    produces:\n    - validated policy document\n    tasks:\n    - id: T-20260802-policy-schema\n      title: Define the versioned rate-limit policy schema\n      goal: Give every downstream stage one valid