uest 101\n      goal: Apply one effective policy at the request boundary without off-by-one drift.\n      done_condition: Requests 1-100 are allowed and request 101 is denied for the same organization window.\n      effort: S\n      profile: standard\n      execution_backend: any\n      required_tools:\n      - git\n      - bash\n      - python3\n      - pytest\n      depends_on:\n      - T-20260802-effective-policy\n      touches_paths: []\n      creates_paths:\n      - src/rate_limit/enforcement.py\n      - tests/test_request_101.py\n      behavior:\n      - id: B-1\n        given: an effective limit of 100 and count 99\n        when: request 100 is evaluated\n        then: the request is allowed\n      - id: B-2\n        given: an effective limit of 100 and count 100\n        when: request 101 is evaluated\n        then: the request is denied exactly once\n      evals:\n      - id: eval_1\n        description: Request 100 remains allowed\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_request_101.py -k request_100\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n      - id: eval_2\n        description: Request 101 is denied\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_request_101.py -k request_101\n        verifies:\n        - B-2\n      - id: eval_3\n        description: The boundary has no off-by-one drift\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_request_101.py -k boundary\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n        - B-2\n      anti_patterns:\n      - action: check the limit after allowing the request\n        reason: request 101 would pass through\n        instead: decide before forwarding work\n      - action: use telemetry as the enforcement source\n        reason: observation is not authorization\n        instead: return an explicit decision from enforcement\n      - action: share counters across organizations\n        reason: one tenant could consume another tenant's budget\n        instead: key state by organization and window\n      do_not_touch:\n      - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n      rollback: Remove the additive enforcement boundary and focused tests.\n      observability: boundary test pass count\n---\n# Request enforcement\n\nSeparates the allow-or-deny decision from response presentation and telemetry.\n\n## Responsibility\n\nApply the effective policy to the organization request count.\n\n## Independent proof\n\nA boundary test allows requests 1 through 100 and denies request 101.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- **Infer enforcement from emitted metrics** — Telemetry observes a decision but cannot authorize or make it.\n\nThis derived seam is ready only while its cited evidence, named owner, contract,\nand rejected alternatives remain intact.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
