{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf43se2yd7nap8QBYtoSh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read the plan artifacts and current CLI state. Here's what the evidence shows.\n\n## Current state first\n\n`taskspec decompose status rate-limit` → `DECOMPOSE=COMPILED`, **accepted tasks 0/4, unproven capabilities 4**. `taskspec ready` returns an empty table, so no leaf is materialized yet. The plan is reviewed and signed (`tasks/.plans/rate-limit/reviews/delivery-plan-review.json`, disposition `accepted`, reviewer `fixture-controller`) — but that review's own reason records \"no leaf execution authorization.\" A plan review is not a leaf seal; nothing here is executed or accepted.\n\n## Why the four are separate\n\nThe separation is not a size split. Every task traces a 1:1 chain **seam → swimlane → leg → task**, and each link carries its own owner, contract, and independent proof (`seam-map.yaml`, `delivery-plan.yaml`).\n\n| Task | Seam / owner | Consumes → produces | Write surface |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `T-20260802-policy-schema` | SEAM-POLICY-CONTRACT / platform-contracts | authored policy → **validated policy document** | `src/rate_limit/policy.schema.json`, `tests/test_policy_schema.py` |\n| `T-20260802-effective-policy` | SEAM-POLICY-RESOLUTION / policy-runtime | validated doc + org identity → **effective policy decision** | `src/rate_limit/policy.py`, `tests/test_policy_resolution.py` |\n| `T-20260802-request-101` | SEAM-REQUEST-ENFORCEMENT / request-runtime | effective policy + count → **allow-or-deny decision** | `src/rate_limit/enforcement.py`, `tests/test_request_101.py` |\n| `T-20260802-decision-visibility` | SEAM-DECISION-VISIBILITY / reliability-interface | allow-or-deny → **visible reason + telemetry event** | `src/rate_limit/decision.py`, `tests/test_decision_visibility.py` |\n\nFour independence tests hold on the current evidence:\n\n- **Distinct authorization boundary** — four different owners, one per seam.\n- **Disjoint write surface** — `creates_paths` do not overlap and every `touches_paths` is `[]`; all four are purely additive, each with its own `rollback`.\n- **Independently assessable completion** — each has its own `done_condition` and three evals bound to its own test file. Schema rejection, precedence, the 101 boundary, and reason/telemetry correlation are each provable without the other three being finished.\n- **Executable size** — all four are `S`, so each is a leaf, not a composition node.\n\nThe seams also record what merging them would destroy. Each `rejected_alternatives` block is the argument against collapsing a boundary: treating the handler as the policy boundary \"would mix contract, resolution, and enforcement\"; resolving policy inside every request adapter would \"drift and become unprovable\"; inferring enforcement from metrics fails because \"telemetry observes a decision but cannot authorize or make it.\" That last one is why enforcement and visibility stay apart rather than shipping as one task.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n`proposed-graph.json` has three `depends_on` edges forming one linear critical path:\n\n```\npolicy-schema → effective-policy → request-101 → decision-visibility\n```\n\nEach edge is contract-carried: the producer's `produces` is exactly the consumer's `requires` at the leg level — validated document, then effective policy decision, then allow-or-deny decision. No edge exists for any other reason, `contentions` is empty, and the order is backed by the accepted `ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER`.\n\nWorth stating plainly: the chain is strictly serial with no fan-out, so this decomposition buys independent ownership and independent proof, **not** parallel execution. Only `policy-schema` is ever the frontier at the start.\n\nThere is deliberately no fifth task for metering. `intent.md` lists \"replacing provider-owned usage metering\" as out of scope, and `OBJ-METERING-SEPARATION` is recorded `FIXED` in both `system-map.md` and `delivery-plan.yaml` — metering was removed from the four-leg proving path and kept external.\n\n## Smallest next action\n\nIf you want these to become real, signed tasks:\n\n```\ntaskspec batch --plan tasks/.plans/rate-limit/task-plan.json\n```\n\nThat materializes the four leaves; it does not accept them. Acceptance still requires evals plus a supervisor signature, and workers cannot sign their own work. I made no changes to the repository."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":645,"cache_read_input_tokens":31441,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":645},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9221baa8-e1b8-4760-9b1d-7da71159e509","uuid":"409585c6-fba0-4b15-8c1c-9e1af90ba0f2","timestamp":"2026-09-14T21:35:24.921Z","request_id":"req_011Cf43sdXhgpAWVAaPydCxv"}
